To time any command we just need to simplt prefix it with time 


eg : time ls 

it will give output like 

real	0m2.002s
user	0m0 001s
sys	0m0 001s


where 
	real : wall clock time : total elapsed time from start to finish
	user : user CPU time : Amount of CPU time spent executing the process in user mode (outside the kernel)
	sys : system CPU time : Amount of CPU time spent inside the kernel on system calls 

Note: total CPU time used by the process is user + sys.  If real < user + sys the command tan across multiple CPU cotrd in parallel
